# The decryption chain and the SpeedLock 7 reader in their plain view ($EC00-$FEE7): the source of src/loader/chain*.asm
# (kit/mkgame.py). tools/speedlock7.py masters the plain view back into the tape bytes.

@module chain ; The decryption chain and the SpeedLock 7 reader
@about The BASIC copies 4840 enciphered bytes to $EC00 and RETs there (CopyChain). Each layer of the chain first wipes the 100 bytes behind it with LDDR, then deciphers the rest of the chain in place with R (set to $45 at the start, so its count is part of the key) and its own constants: ADD / SUB / XOR with a running byte, or keyed by its own address (a CALL whose callee POPs the return address into IX and mixes IXH and IXL into each byte, then leaves through JP (IX) whose $DD,$E9 bytes the next layer leaves as data). tools/speedlock7.py follows the 119 rewrites; this view holds every layer as it runs.
@about The last layer leaves the SpeedLock 7 reader at $FB7E: it checks the ROM ($0000 must be $F3), silences the interface ports, clears the RAM and the screen, then loads the second stage (TZX block 7) to $FEE8 with its own edge timing and a 7-pulse sync pattern.
$EC00 c ChainStart ; The first layer: R = $45, wipe behind, decipher $12B4 bytes keyed by the CALL's return address
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$EC18 c LayerKeyed01 ; A keyed layer: POP IX (its return address) + 28, then each byte = ((R XOR IXH) - byte) XOR IXL
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$EC6F b LayerExit01 ; $DD,$E9: the JP (IX) the keyed layer leaves through, as the next layer leaves it (deciphered after it ran)
$EC71 c Layer02 ; The next layers: wipe the 100 bytes behind, decipher the rest with R and a running byte
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$ECA7 c LayerKeyed03 ; A keyed layer: POP IX (its return address) + 28, then each byte = ((R XOR IXH) - byte) XOR IXL
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
