$FB62 c LayerKeyed46 ; A keyed layer: POP IX (its return address) + 28, then each byte = ((R XOR IXH) - byte) XOR IXL
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$FB7E SL7Start ; the reader: the ROM check ($0000 = $F3), the ports $1F, $7B, $BB, $7F, the RAM cleared
$FBCB c SL7WipeTrap ; Zero memory upward from $FBD7 for ever: the end of a failed check
> No recording ran it: known only from the code (the load passed every check).
$FBD7 c SL7Reveal ; The per-bit hook: while $82FF is set, LDI 12 bytes from $8000 to the attributes a step (the screen revealed as it loads)
> Witness: L1 57161 (c1).
$FCD1 b SL7Bytes ; four bytes $90, $98, $80, $90 between the routines
$FCD5 c SL7Edge2 ; Wait for two edges
> Witness: L1 282 (c1).
$FCD9 c SL7Edge1 ; Wait for one edge after the standard delay
> Witness: L1 3292 (c1).
$FCDB c SL7EdgeDelay ; Delay A, then wait for an edge on EAR counting B; carry when found, the border striped
> Witness: L1 2521777 (c1).
$FCF6 c SL7LoadBlock ; Load DE bytes to IX: the pilot, the sync and the 7-pulse pattern of SL7Pattern, then the bytes through the store hook
> Witness: L1 2 (c1).
$FDB3 b SL7StoreHook ; The byte store stage 2 points the reader at ($FDB1 = $FDB3): LD A,$C1 / XOR L / ADD A,$11 / LD (IX+0),A ...; bytes in this view (known only from the code)
$FDC7 c SL7Blocks ; Walk the block table at IY: 5-byte records (address, length, the $7FFD bank or 0), each block loaded with SL7LoadBlock's bit loop
> Witness: L1 7 (c1).
$FE2A c SL7ReadBit ; Read one bit into L (the edge time against $DB)
> Witness: L1 147 (c1).
$FE40 c SL7LoadStage2 ; Load the next stage, then sample the EAR line 255 times into $9000 and check it unless $006D holds $28
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$FE5B c SL7CountEdges ; Count the EAR changes in 255 loops into E
> Witness: L1 255 (c1).
$FE77 c SL7CheckSamples ; Sum two runs of 50 samples; a bad pair sets SL7Pattern's flag byte
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$FEB3 b SL7Pattern ; The flag byte (non-zero: a failed check, the reader wipes memory) and the 7 sync pulse limits (pairs)
$FEC2 c SL7BlockEnd ; After a block: border black; a bad block wipes memory (SL7WipeTrap)
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$FECD SL7Main ; SP = $FFFF, the screen cleared, the second stage (232 bytes) loaded to $FEE8
